---
/**
 * TODO(client): this policy is accurate to what the site actually does, but a
 * published privacy policy needs the registered legal entity name, registered
 * address, and a decision on whether a Data Protection Officer is named. Those
 * are marked inline below. Have it reviewed before launch — the site collects
 * personal data from creators and brands in the EU, so GDPR applies.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../consts';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How AMAVI Socials collects, uses and stores personal data from brands and creators, and the rights you have under GDPR."
>
  <section class="section page-head">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1 class="display display--lg">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta page-head__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="policy">
        <p class="policy__lead">
          This policy explains what personal data {SITE_NAME} collects through this
          website, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and what you can ask us to do
          with it. It applies to both brands making an enquiry and creators joining our
          network.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} is an influencer marketing agency operating in Ireland. For the
          purposes of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) we are the data
          controller for the information described below.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): insert the registered legal entity name, company registration
          number and registered address. A published policy needs all three.]
        </p>
        <p>
          You can reach us about anything in this policy at
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

        <h3>If you make an enquiry as a brand</h3>
        <p>
          Through the form on our Work With Us page we collect your name, company, email
          address, the service you are interested in, an optional budget range, and
          whatever you write in the message field.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this solely to respond to your enquiry and to discuss working together.
          Our lawful basis is your consent, given when you tick the box on the form. We
          do not add enquiry contacts to a mailing list.
        </p>

        <h3>If you join the creator network</h3>
        <p>
          Through the form on our Creators page we collect your name, email address, city
          and country, links to your social channels, your follower range, your
          engagement rate, your niches, your collaboration preference, the content
          formats you produce, your rates and any notes on them, any audience insights
          you choose to share, details of past collaborations, a media kit link, and any
          other notes you add.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this to maintain our creator database and to match creators to client
          briefs. <strong>We share these details with our clients</strong> when we are
          considering you for a collaboration — that is the purpose of the database, and
          it is what the consent checkbox on the form covers. Our lawful basis is your
          consent.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Brand enquiries are kept for as long as we are in active conversation with you,
          and for a reasonable period afterwards in case the conversation resumes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Creator details are kept in our database until you ask us to remove them. We do
          not set an automatic expiry, because the value of the database to you is that
          we can come to you when something fits, potentially years after you sign up.
          You can ask us to delete your details at any time.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): if you want a fixed retention period instead — for example,
          reviewing creator records every 24 months — state it here.]
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Our clients.</strong> Creator details are shared with the brands we
            represent, for the purpose of considering you for collaborations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Netlify.</strong> This site is hosted by Netlify, and both forms are
            processed through Netlify Forms. Form submissions pass through and are stored
            on their infrastructure.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it with anyone else for their
          own marketing purposes.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): if an analytics tool, CRM or email platform is added, list it
          here. If a tool transfers data outside the EEA, that transfer and its safeguard
          must be named.]
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets no cookies of its own and uses no advertising or tracking
          cookies. Because nothing non-essential is set, no cookie banner is shown.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): analytics has not been added yet. If GA4 is chosen it sets
          cookies and a consent banner becomes legally required before it loads. A
          cookieless tool such as Plausible would not change this section.]
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
          <li>ask us to correct anything inaccurate;</li>
          <li>ask us to delete your data;</li>
          <li>ask us to restrict how we use it;</li>
          <li>ask us to transfer it to you or another provider;</li>
          <li>object to our use of it; and</li>
          <li>
            withdraw your consent at any time, which stops any further use without
            affecting what was lawful beforehand.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these, email
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We will respond within
          one month.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe we have handled your data improperly, you can complain to the
          Irish Data Protection Commission at
          <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dataprotection.ie</a>.
          We would rather you came to us first so we can put it right.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle personal data we will update this page and change
          the date at the top.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .page-head__meta { margin-top: var(--space-s); }

  .policy { max-width: var(--measure); }

  .policy__lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-l);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--display-sm);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .policy h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .policy p { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .policy p + p { margin-top: var(--space-s); }
  .policy strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .policy a { color: var(--accent-alt); }

  .policy ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .policy li {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    position: relative;
  }
  .policy li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; top: 0.75em;
    width: 0.5em; height: 1px;
    background: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* Visible on purpose: these are unresolved and must not ship unnoticed. */
  .policy__todo {
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-alt);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink) !important;
  }
</style>
